    "body": "Cause: `machining3d::pocket3d_air_split` (the rotary wrap ladder) rewrote Adaptive to OffsetRings before running the level ladder (M11.4 pin), so no developed level ever reached `hsm::plan_level`.\n\nPlan: drop the pin - the wrap ladder already runs the planar `ladder` -> `hsm::plan_level` per level, and `wrap_exit` already chords every developed arc before wrapping. Add a seam law (`hsm::Seam`, threaded through `ladder`/`plan_level`, built per leg from its cover's s-ends, period 2πR_ref, reach = 2·(r+leave)): a level centre component that reaches a cover end but spans less than a full period is an area the seam cuts, not a wall of the work -> Adaptive refused by name for that level, Offset rings cut it, radius named. Full-lap bands keep the seam pad law and are planned. Planner refusals on the wrap name the level as 'the developed level at radius R'. OffsetRings untouched (digest-pinned). Tests: new motion suite `rotary_adaptive` (load/kink on the developed path, radial poses, rings digest, seam refusal) + app rotary_verify/rotary_fixtures/golden_cl/operations.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
