    "body": "Box ran out before it could be proven; nothing staged (WIP left unstaged in agent worktree agent-aa81749c90ed1a4dd).\n\nWhat I found with the pin lifted and the seam law added (motion suite `rotary_adaptive`, turned bar r6/r5 neck in an r6.2 stock, BN D6, leave 0.5, stepdown 0.5, Plunge entry):\n- radius 6.200: HSM-planned, 29,954 planar moves, 1,258 proved arcs, 0 breaks past 5°. The **planner itself** reports a 76.8% D peak at the tool-size axial bore (424% over the 14.6% law; 'no spiral step holds the load', Plunge entry). My test's 0.0% D reading was an artifact: the measuring stock top sat at that level's own radius (zero depth). So the load law is **not** shown to hold yet; a Helix entry, or the bore placed where the stock is already open, is the likely fix.\n- radius 5.700 / 5.200: the planner refused them by name (out-of-cut travel over 1.5x) and Offset rings cut them, each note naming its radius. The named-radius refusal works.\n- OffsetRings digest (5194 moves, FNV 6097177489831100083), from code whose rings path is unchanged. Not yet checked against a HEAD build.\n- Seam fixture: a D-flat r6 bar is refused earlier by the axis fit (the 'every axis fits' sphere guard), so the seam refusal has no passing test yet. A longer bar would get past that guard.\n- Cost: the Adaptive test took about 10 min in debug, so it belongs in the heavy lane (#[ignore], release).",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
